description:
FILED s526w1 (Opus, 2026-10-24) from the URI-5.34 board census (t/heuristic.t rows 7 and 9).  PRE-EXISTING (main 761d92f4 gives the same).

A `BEGIN { *CORE::GLOBAL::NAME = sub {...} }` in the MAIN program does not reach a built-in call inside a MODULE `use`d after it.  perl decides the override when it compiles the call, so a module compiled after the BEGIN calls the override; PCL decides it statically per compilation unit (the module's own transpile -- and its cached copy -- cannot know what the program installed).

REPRO (scratch/s526w1/pr/gh.pl + pr/lib/GhMod.pm):
    # lib/GhMod.pm
    package GhMod; sub look { gethostbyname($_[0]) ? "yes" : "no" } 1;
    # gh.pl
    BEGIN { *CORE::GLOBAL::gethostbyname = sub { $_[0] eq "mocked.invalid." ? 1 : 0 } }
    use lib "scratch/s526w1/pr/lib"; use GhMod;
    print GhMod::look("mocked.invalid."), " ", GhMod::look("localhost"), "\n";
  perl 5.40.3: yes no
  PCL (base and tree): no yes

docs/not-supported.md "Builtin override: only the COMPILE-TIME spellings" lists the BEGIN spelling as WORKING -- true within one unit, not across a module boundary, so the entry needs this case either way.  Consumer: URI t/heuristic.t mocks gethostbyname to test URI::Heuristic's guessing (2 rows); any test that mocks a built-in for the module under test (time, sleep, gethostbyname, ...) has this shape.  A fix needs the override to be a RUNTIME dispatch for the built-ins a CORE::GLOBAL can replace (the cached module emission cannot carry it) -- size it against the per-call cost first.
